    "description": "The Procrastinatory Cognitions Inventory (PCI) is an 18-item self-report scale measuring the frequency of automatic thoughts associated with task avoidance and delay. It is used in cognitive-behavioral research and clinical assessment to identify the cognitive patterns that sustain procrastinatory behavior.",
